        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The sunburst square works "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "double treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " spikes back into the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in round 2, producing tall spikes that radiate inward toward the centre and stand above the surrounding "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "trebles"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of round 1. Working into the ring rather than into the round-1 stitches pulls the spike bases toward the centre, giving a true starburst appearance. Rounds 3 and 4 return to standard granny construction, so the square edges are conventional and compatible with any granny blanket."
          }
        ]
      },
