      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Note: ch 3 counts as first tr throughout rounds 1, 3, and 4. Double treble (dtr): yarn over three times, insert hook, (yarn over, pull through 2 loops) four times."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 11 tr into the ring. Pull tail to close. Join with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sl st"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to top of ch 3. (12 tr.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2 (spike round)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "*Ch 1. Work 1 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dtr"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " directly into the magic ring (pushing your hook into the ring itself, not into a stitch). Ch 1. Sl st into the next tr of round 1*; repeat from * to * 11 more times (12 repeats total). Each sl st anchors the spike to the round-1 treble, and each dtr stands above as a spike leaning back toward the centre. (12 dtr spikes.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work this round into the spaces between the spike bases, at the level of round 1. Join yarn to the space between two spikes at a corner position. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). *(2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into the corner space (standard granny corner). Ch 1. 3 tr into the side space between the next pair of spikes. Ch 1*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. Join with sl st to top of ch 3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 sides.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) into corner sp. Ch 1. 3 tr into ch-1 side sp. Ch 1. 3 tr into next ch-1 side sp. Ch 1*; repeat from * to * 3 more times. Join with sl st to top of ch 3. Fasten off. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 8 ch-1 side sps.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-sunburst-square"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in tails carefully; the spike round creates extra thread ends at the ring. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Block"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flat with the four corners pinned to 90 degrees. The spikes will remain slightly raised from the face of the motif even when blocked; this is the intended texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The outer rounds are standard granny construction, so sunburst squares join to any other granny square using the same sl st or whip-stitch methods. The spike centre is contained within rounds 1 and 2 and does not affect joining."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash in cool water. Lay flat to dry. The dtr spikes are robust and hold their shape well after washing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The puff stitch square uses a similarly raised central element placed at the sides rather than the centre. For a pure spike motif without the granny square border, the six-point star works the same principle of radiating increases in a round format."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
